#: ../../../explanation/security/snapd-release-process.md:2
msgid "Snapd release process"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/snapd-release-process.md:4
msgid ""
"The snapd release process is maintained in the snapd repository. It is "
"written primarily for release engineers on the snapd team, and it is "
"published for transparency. Carrying out a release requires administrative "
"privileges that most people do not have."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/snapd-release-process.md:6
msgid "Release planning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/snapd-release-process.md:8
msgid ""
"At the start of every six-month cycle, snapd agrees a release plan with "
"stakeholders. The plan gives estimated start and end dates for each release, "
"and those dates determine what the release contains. The process is date-"
"driven: if you want a change in a particular release, it needs to fit that "
"plan."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/snapd-release-process.md:10
msgid "Release artifacts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/snapd-release-process.md:12
msgid "A release produces:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/snapd-release-process.md:14
msgid ""
"The [snapd snap](https://snapcraft.io/snapd), as a regular build and a FIPS "
"build"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/snapd-release-process.md:15
msgid "[snapd Debian packages](https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/snapd/)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/snapd-release-process.md:16
msgid "A [GitHub release](https://github.com/canonical/snapd/releases)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/snapd-release-process.md:17
msgid ""
"{ref}`Cross-distro artifacts <reference-administration-distribution-support>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/snapd-release-process.md:19
msgid "Security releases"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/snapd-release-process.md:21
msgid ""
"Security releases are prepared in private. They address vulnerabilities "
"identified during routine security scanning and through external reports. To "
"report a suspected vulnerability, see {ref}`How to report vulnerabilities "
"<explanation-security-security-policies-how-to-report-vulnerabilities>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/snapd-release-process.md:23
msgid "Ubuntu package updates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/snapd-release-process.md:25
msgid ""
"Updates of the snapd Debian package in Ubuntu follow a package-specific, non-"
"standard Stable Release Update (SRU) process. The [snapd SRU exception] "
"documents where that process deviates from the standard SRU process. A "
"refresh of that documentation is in progress and is expected to become "
"available by November 2026."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/snapd-release-process.md:27
msgid "Full process"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/security/snapd-release-process.md:29
msgid ""
"For the step-by-step release process, follow the instructions in "
"[RELEASE.md]."
msgstr ""
